 <iati-activity default-currency="USD" hierarchy="1" iati-activities:version="2.03" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities">
  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-KIR102</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved partnerships, workers and vulnerable groups are effectively protected   from unacceptable forms of work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancement of fair and effective labor migration policies and measures at the regional and national level are crucial in the context of Kiribati, where there is a need to protect the rights of migrant workers and ensure their safe and secure working environments. The ILO has previously provided technical assistance in development of the National Action Plan (NAP) on the reintegration of returned migrant workers in Kiribati.
The ILO, in partnership with the US-funded MCC and the Government of Kiribati, is managing Activity 2 (MARI 2) valued at about US$6m. The project, in collaboration with MEHR, aims to support Kiribati workers and their families in securing overseas employment. It plans to establish a resource center for pre-departure and reintegration support. The project office was set up in June 2024 in Tarawa but is currently on hold due to the US executive order.
During the current biennium, the ILO&apos;s efforts aim to strengthen labor migration governance, protect migrant workers&apos; rights, and promote safe and secure working environments for all workers in the region through the Pacific Regional Labour Mobility  Priniciples.</narrative>
  </description>
